+# Incidents brief: August–September 2026
+
+Status as of the 30 September on-call meeting.
+
+## 11 August: ingest stall and full database disk
+
+**Impact:** Customer dashboards were stale for about 2.5 hours overnight; no data lost.
+
+**Root cause:** One malformed batch jammed the ingest pipeline; its endless retries flooded the logs and filled the database disk, which then refused writes.
+
+**Fix:** A restart that set the bad batch aside, then database cleanup and log compression.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Disk alert at 80% (Sunil): done.
+- Stop bad batches jamming the pipeline (Jonas): open, in review.
+- Faster paging escalation (Elif): done; unanswered pages escalate after 15 minutes.
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+**Impact:** For 47 minutes, browsers and nearly all API clients could not connect.
+
+**Root cause:** The API's security certificate expired. Its automatic renewal had failed silently since early September, using an outdated credential.
+
+**Fix:** Certificate renewed and API restarted. The renewal job now has the current credential and alerts on failure.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Reminder 14 days before expiry (Priya): done.
+- Alert on days until expiry (Priya): open.
+- Expiry check in weekly checklist (Tomasz): open.
+- Responders record their steps during incidents (Mara): done, in on-call handover notes.
